<p><strong>Seeking Greenlights:</strong> Yes</p>
<p><strong>Page Type:</strong> SCP Article.</p>
<p><strong>Genre:</strong> Not decided yet.<br />
<strong>Page Layout:</strong> I will use a normal type of layout (I don't know too much how to edit the layout), but I will separate the many types of pages of the SCP.<br />
<strong>Elevator Pitch:</strong></p>
<ul>
<li>Blanks-torn pages encounter all over the world, if someone grabs a page it will show a comic of different moments in your life depending on which page you grab.</li>
<li>The pages show moments with relations with emotions, for example, one page will show the happiest moment in your life, another one will show the angriest moment, etc.</li>
<li>The style of drawing of the comic will depend on the own style and knowledge of the person holding the page.</li>
</ul>
<p><strong>Central Narrative:</strong> The pages are spread all over the world and each page will show a different moment if all the pages are found it will be possible for the pages to show a short version of your life in form of a comic.<br />
The first page the foundation encounters was the page that shows the happiest moment of your life, a circus has an attraction that says &quot;revive the happiest moment of your life&quot; the people that go to the attraction always get out with great enthusiasm, the foundation decided to investigate thinking it was any form of drug or special ability of an anomalous human, but it was a simple page that shows a comic when it is holding it after it was discovered another page in another country this time the page shows the hungriest moment after this many others pages are being found, but the foundation thinks that are many more pages hiding around the world.<br />
The pages can be used to know more things about certain SCP.<br />
The origins are not certain, but the foundation wants to find all the pages as quickly as possible.<br />
<strong>Hook/Attention-Grabber:</strong> The principal theme of this SCP is the discovery of the most important moments in your life and how this can affect your way to see the world and see you, and how knowing or remember again these moments can affect you.</p>
<p><strong>Additional Notes:</strong> I have not to make a draft yet, but the article will have two images taken from me I get greenlighted.</p>

