														</div>
			</div>
			<div class="content" id="post-content-4828733">
									

<p><strong>Seeking Greenlights:</strong> Yes, but I don’t expect it’ll get greenlit at the first go. I’m mostly looking for feedback right now.</p>
<p><strong>Page Type:</strong> SCP Article</p>
<p><strong>Genre (optional):</strong> Unsure</p>
<p><strong>Page Layout (optional):</strong> Contains containment procedures, description, discovery, test logs, and maybe even a cross-link.</p>
<p><strong>Elevator Pitch:</strong> A “living” carved wooden vulture that feeds on human corpses. It will get “hungry” after 24 hours, which is when it will start searching for corpses to feed on. If it hasn't eaten for 36 to 48 hours, it will enter a frenzy, which makes it exponentially stronger and more aggressive. In this state, it will eat people alive in order to satiate its “hunger.” In this state, it will even ignore any dead human meat and go straight for the nearest living human.</p>
<p><strong>Central Narrative:</strong> What is speculated to be its first victim was a woodworker specializing in custom statues. It's believed that the vulture killed the victim as opposed to feasting on their corpse.</p>
<p>Ever since the first body was found, mutilated and dismembered, many more bodies soon popped up with similar disfigurements. This caused many problems for local law enforcement.</p>
<p>The Foundation stepped in when a video of the creature was brought into the hands of the police. What caught their eye was the unnatural material it seemed to be made out of.</p>
<p>The Foundation easily caught it with the scent of human flesh, but they did not fully understand its eating habits at the time, nor did they anticipate the consequences of the lack of understanding that they had. They tried to feed it animal carcasses. They were able to keep it for 2 days before it escaped in one of its “frenzy states” and ate a facility guard alive. It was soon recaptured and given human flesh to eat. It hasn't escaped, nor tried to escape since then.</p>
<p>Presently, the SCP sits in its containment cell, docile. It is given a pound of human flesh every 24 hours. It seems to be satiated.</p>
<p><strong>Hook/Attention-Grabber:</strong> The simple but unique appearance and description combined with the grotesque nature of its feeding.</p>
<p><strong>Additional Notes:</strong> “How's The Foundation able to obtain the human flesh that they feed the SCP?”</p>
<p>The Foundation has struck a deal with a nearby city using one of their front companies, which allows them access to unwanted or unclaimed dead bodies. They also have access to the corpses of people who have donated their bodies to science.</p>
<p>I’d be willing to delete the “escaped and ate a guard” part to make The Foundation not look like idiots.</p>
<p>If this ever gets greenlit I’d like to include a brief cross-link to <a href="/scp-3847">SCP-3847</a> if possible.</p>

							</div>

								
					
